=⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{t}^{5}}{5}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{4},\\,6t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4{t}^{3},\\,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
